title: OverflowingTextWithTooltip
description: Truncate long text and reveal its full value in a tooltip.
---

import { PageBanner } from "/snippets/page-banner.mdx"

import { StoryEmbed } from '/snippets/ui/StoryEmbed.mdx';

import OverflowingTextWithTooltipReference from '/snippets/ui/generated/typography/overflowing-text-with-tooltip.mdx';

## Overview

`OverflowingTextWithTooltip` truncates content within the available width. It checks for overflow on pointer entry and focus, then shows a tooltip only when needed. It manages tooltip visibility internally and exposes no controlled or uncontrolled open-state props. Use [OverflowingTextTooltipModeProvider](/ui/primitives/typography/overflowing-text-tooltip-mode-provider) to change when a subtree checks truncation or to turn the tooltip off.

<StoryEmbed
  storyId="ui-surfaces-overflowingtextwithtooltip--display"
  title="OverflowingTextWithTooltip example"
  height={180}
/>

## Usage

```tsx
import {
  OverflowingTextWithTooltip,
  Text,
} from 'twenty-ui/primitives/typography';

export const RecordTitle = () => (
  <Text style={{ maxWidth: 220 }}>
    <OverflowingTextWithTooltip
      text="Quarterly account review and renewal preparation"
      isFocusable
    />
  </Text>
);
```

Constrain the width of the surrounding layout so truncation can occur. `isFocusable` gives the text a tab stop and opens the tooltip on focus or click. Keep essential information available to users who cannot hover.

## Choose typography

`size`, `weight` and `color` match [Text](/ui/primitives/typography/text). They are optional and inherit independently when omitted. Explicit typography applies to the displayed text; the tooltip retains its shared appearance.

```tsx
import { OverflowingTextWithTooltip } from 'twenty-ui/primitives/typography';

export const WorkspaceCaption = () => (
  <OverflowingTextWithTooltip
    text="Quarterly account review and renewal preparation"
    size="xs"
    weight="semibold"
    color="light"
    style={{ maxWidth: 220 }}
  />
);
```

## Multiline content

```tsx
import {
  OverflowingTextWithTooltip,
  Text,
} from 'twenty-ui/primitives/typography';

export const RecordDescription = () => (
  <Text style={{ maxWidth: 220 }}>
    <OverflowingTextWithTooltip
      text="Review the account history, confirm the renewal date, and prepare the next conversation with the customer."
      lineClamp={2}
      isTooltipMultiline
      isFocusable
    />
  </Text>
);
```

`lineClamp` matches Text and limits the displayed lines; use a positive integer. `isTooltipMultiline` preserves whitespace and line breaks inside the tooltip. Without a row limit, text truncates on one line.

## Custom content and timing

```tsx
import {
  OverflowingTextWithTooltip,
  Text,
} from 'twenty-ui/primitives/typography';

export const ImportResult = () => (
  <Text style={{ maxWidth: 220 }}>
    <OverflowingTextWithTooltip
      text={<strong>24 records imported successfully</strong>}
      tooltipContent="24 records imported successfully"
      tooltipPlace="top"
      tooltipDelay={300}
      isFocusable
    />
  </Text>
);
```

React content requires a plain-string `tooltipContent`. With string text, that prop can override the tooltip label; otherwise the text itself is used. An empty or missing label does not open a tooltip. String URLs remain plain text. Supply links explicitly in `text` or through `render`. Link content and navigation stay caller-owned.

`alwaysShowTooltip` allows the tooltip even without truncation. `tooltipDelay` controls the hover delay and defaults to 500 milliseconds. `tooltipPlace` defaults to `bottom`.

Native attributes, styles, class names, event handlers, and refs target the displayed Text element, a `div` by default. `render` can replace that element while retaining truncation and tooltip behavior. `OverflowingTextWithTooltipProps` is exported from `twenty-ui/primitives/typography`. Typography inherits from the surrounding layout unless an explicit typography prop is supplied. Set `truncate={false}` to wrap; choose either `truncate` or `lineClamp`. Focusable rendered elements and a caller-supplied `tabIndex` also reveal the tooltip on focus. Use [Text](/ui/primitives/typography/text) and [Tooltip](/ui/primitives/surfaces/tooltip) directly when you need custom composition. Interactive popup content belongs in [Popover](/ui/primitives/surfaces/popover).

## Explicit links

```tsx
import { OverflowingTextWithTooltip } from 'twenty-ui/primitives/typography';

export const DocumentationLink = () => (
  <OverflowingTextWithTooltip
    text="https://twenty.com/developers"
    render={
      <a href="https://twenty.com/developers" aria-label="Documentation" />
    }
    style={{ maxWidth: 160, display: 'block' }}
  />
);
```

Use a single anchor for the whole label, or supply individual anchors in React content with a plain `tooltipContent`. The component adds no anchors of its own. Keep tooltip content informational.

## Migration

Replace `displayedMaxRows` with `lineClamp`. The former `size="small"` and `size="large"` options controlled height, not font size. `large` set a 16px height. The new `size` selects theme font sizes and accepts no legacy aliases; use native `style` or `className` for height constraints. `color` now accepts semantic colors; move arbitrary CSS colors to `style={{ color: customColor }}`. Move intentional URL recognition into caller-owned content. No automatic linkification remains in this component.

