---
title: Chip
description: Show compact caller-owned content with optional leading and trailing slots.
---

import { PageBanner } from "/snippets/page-banner.mdx"

import { StoryEmbed } from '/snippets/ui/StoryEmbed.mdx';

import ChipReference from '/snippets/ui/generated/data-display/chip.mdx';

## Overview

Use `Chip` for compact references to people, records, or files. Use [Tag](/ui/primitives/data-display/tag) for colored categories and [Status](/ui/primitives/data-display/status) for workflow states.

<StoryEmbed
  storyId="ui-data-display-chip--display"
  title="Chip example"
  height={90}
/>

## Usage

```tsx
import { Avatar, Chip } from 'twenty-ui/primitives/data-display';

export const AssigneeChip = () => (
  <Chip
    variant="soft"
    startElement={
      <Avatar name="Jane" size="sm" shape="circle" imageProps={{ alt: '' }} />
    }
  >
    Jane
  </Chip>
);
```

Children accept text or nodes. `startElement` and `endElement` accept avatars, icons, or other content. `endElementDivider` adds a separator before the trailing content. The default chip is a `div`; its slots can contain a separate action while the chip itself remains presentational.

Chip never inserts a label. Supply a translated fallback from your application when needed. Omit children for content made entirely from slots. An interactive chip with only an icon needs a caller-supplied accessible name.

## Appearance

<StoryEmbed
  storyId="ui-data-display-chip--catalog"
  title="Chip variants and sizes"
  height={200}
/>

`size` accepts `sm` or `md`, with total heights of 20px and 24px. `variant` accepts `ghost`, `soft`, `solid`, `plain`, or `outline`; `ghost` is the default. Plain chips have no resting fill or leading padding. Outline chips have a strong 1px border, a lighter resting fill, and 8px inline padding on each side, with the same total height as other variants. Clickable plain and outline chips use the ghost hover and pressed backgrounds, pointer cursor, and focus ring. Use `shape="round"` for a pill, `weight="medium"` for emphasis, and `color="secondary"` for secondary text.

## Buttons and links

```tsx
import { Avatar, Chip } from 'twenty-ui/primitives/data-display';

type AssigneeActionProps = {
  onOpenAssignee: () => void;
  disabled?: boolean;
};

export const AssigneeAction = ({
  onOpenAssignee,
  disabled,
}: AssigneeActionProps) => (
  <Chip
    render={<button type="button" disabled={disabled} />}
    onClick={onOpenAssignee}
    aria-label="Open Jane's record"
    startElement={
      <Avatar name="Jane" size="sm" shape="circle" imageProps={{ alt: '' }} />
    }
  >
    Jane
  </Chip>
);
```

Supplying `onClick` keeps the default `div`. Use `render` to compose an explicit native button, anchor, router link, or another appropriate owner. Native attributes, handlers, styles and the root ref reach that owner. A native button supplies keyboard activation and disabled behavior. Chip recognizes native disabled state and `aria-disabled` for appearance; `aria-disabled` alone does not prevent activation.

`clickable` controls hover and pointer appearance and defaults to whether `onClick` is supplied. Set it explicitly for a link without a click handler. Do not nest buttons or links inside a chip that is itself interactive.

```tsx
import { Chip } from 'twenty-ui/primitives/data-display';

export const DocumentationChip = () => (
  <Chip
    variant="outline"
    shape="round"
    render={<a href="https://twenty.com/developers" />}
    clickable
  >
    Documentation
  </Chip>
);
```

URL text remains plain text. Intentional links belong in caller content or in the explicit root composition.

## Truncation and tooltips

```tsx
import { Chip } from 'twenty-ui/primitives/data-display';

export const FileChip = () => (
  <Chip variant="soft" maxWidth={180} tooltipPlace="top">
    Quarterly customer research.pdf
  </Chip>
);
```

`maxWidth` constrains the rendered chip width in pixels, including padding and any outline border. The same limit applies to plain chips with asymmetric padding. Content truncates with an ellipsis by default; `truncate={false}` leaves it unconstrained by truncation. String children supply their own tooltip text. Set `tooltipContent` for custom text or node content, `tooltipDelay` for the opening delay, and `isTooltipMultiline` to preserve line breaks. `alwaysShowTooltip` also enables the tooltip when content fits. These options follow [OverflowingTextWithTooltip](/ui/primitives/typography/overflowing-text-with-tooltip). Keep essential information available without relying on hover.

## Migration

Replace `emptyLabel` with caller-provided fallback children, and replace `forceEmptyText` or `isLabelHidden` with omitted children. Keep translated product fallbacks in the application. Replace `tooltipLabel` with `tooltipContent`. Move `disabled` to the explicit interactive owner and remove `nativeButton`. Add a native button or link through `render` wherever the chip previously relied on `onClick` to choose its element.

Replace leading-padding overrides with `variant="plain"`. Keep `clickable` enabled for native links and buttons that need hover and pressed feedback.

## Props

Types and defaults are generated from the public component types. Native attributes and event handlers are also accepted.

